@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] boot-log-no-elevation-or-payload-diagnostics
The logger MUST run without setuid bits or file capabilities, invoke the command
directly without a shell, and persist only the bounded boot log file. Child
payload bytes reach the private log file only; they never become messages on
the helper's own stdout, stderr or any diagnostic stream.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] boot-log-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover selector refusal, the output-custody refusal
matrix, exact bounded retention across generated sizes, chunking-independent
line timestamps against an independent oracle, child exit/signal
mapping and nonblocking discard under flood. Real custody invariants keep
process-level fixtures; no root or KVM is required.
